  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nMainly dry conditions are expected to continue through the remainder \nof the week and beginning of the weekend. A cold front will \nglide east across the forecast area overnight tonight. Most of \nthe forecast area will remain dry with the frontal passage \noutside of low-end PoPs in lake enhanced rain showers across \nNorthwest Pennsylvania tonight. Another area of high pressure \nbuilds overhead behind the cold front leading to prolonged dry \nconditions through late Saturday. High temperatures Thursday and\nFriday will be cooler in the upper 60s to lower 70s. A warm \nfront will lift across the Upper Ohio Valley on Saturday leading\nto high temperatures in mid 70s to low 80s. Lows will generally\nfall into the low 50s tonight and Saturday night. Chillier on\nFriday night with lows in the mid 40s.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\nUnsettled weather returns Sunday and continues into the middle of \nnext week. Tropical Storm Isaias currently located in the \nsouthwestern Gulf is expected to make landfall as a hurricane \nlater this week along the northern Gulf coast. The remmants of \nIsaias will move northward into the Tennessee and Ohio Valley \nand bring widespread rainfall to the region on Sunday. Current \nforecast is dry for Monday before an upper trough digs eastward \nacross the Great Lakes region Tuesday into Wednesday bringing \nrenewed rain chances.",
